Yes true. AFAICT, the conversion protocol is _only_ called for from
the sacrificing code, not from praying.

You get converted when sacrificing something on a cross-aligned altar
while your alignment is "strayed" or worse or when the sacrifice is a
unicorn of your own alignment[1]. 
In either case, your original deity will refuse to accept the
sacrifice, but the altar's god will accept your gift and thus your
allegiance.

[1] How do i know? I've done that myself, and more than once on
purpose. 
The unicorn trick is by far the easiest method.

> What you can do is sacrifice more (non-human) corpses here on *this* altar
> to convert it back to Toth.

Unless you can verify that your current alignment is still sufficient
(not guaranteed after a same-species sacrifice on Thoth's altar and a
prayer to a rival god), that's a bit of a gamble.

